      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "An initiative for approved and trusted mods would definitely be nice, as some definitely add nice features.  For example, global dynamic bones makes things much more immersive.\nPerhaps there could even be an initiative to review mod added features and make said features present in unmodded VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-09T23:40:19.153Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "so we all know that mods are takin as \"oh but what about stolen avatars and accounts\" but hear me out what if the safety team didnt have to worry and as well as the dev team didnt have to worry about the specific of these mods. Lets say for example that if we were to classify the mods as User Created Content/Addons, within like the vrchat could add a list of Addons users have created for content within the server and allow them to use that opportunity in game(not all mods should be used). The reason why im wanting this to be added within vrchat is because mods have been a thing in vrchat since 2018 and so far it hasnt changed or so ive seen so i wanted the safety team to look at these mods or User Created Content add ons and go over them to see which ones will work and which ones wont work. Also yes as we call it mods which go against VRChats ToS when in fact if we called them UcC (User Created Content) it wouldnt be breaking ToS because using unity to make avatars, worlds, etc, is defined as User Created content. I want the player to be able to use these add ons by the safety team and not be ridiculed because the whole team says no. people get bullied because they cant use them i have witnessed this issue as well.",
